INSERT INTO feature VALUES('total-parsing','syntax','Total, error-tolerant parsing',NULL,'implemented','notable',NULL,'Every source parses to a molded tree, an unfinished form left open with the completion obligations that would close it. A `)` or a `]` the source left out is minted where it closes its form and the rest of its top-level form then parses — the last such place of the melder''s close and the tile ends after the form''s last written tile — and the repairs its misreading made fall away; the minted close reaches back to the first such place, and the close is refused over every place between. Any other tile left out — a member''s `;`, an arm''s `=>`, a binder''s `:` or a `,` — is minted the same way for the deepest form missing one or the first, directly after the form''s last written tile when no hole comes between them, else at a later tile end outside the brackets opened since and never inside a word, where the rest parses with every tile before it read as written, every top-level form a declaration and the form nested no deeper. A top-level form whose declaration keyword is left out or misspelled, read as an expression, is read again with each keyword its first tile can follow written before it, and the first that makes it a declaration with no repair is the parse, the keyword minted at its head and owed alone. A `,` left out before a line at its group''s items'' column is minted at the end of the line the item leaves when the parse then owes fewer obligations, with the group''s closer before it when the line comes back to the group''s limit and the top-level form then owes nothing. A `,` left out between two operands side by side in a group is minted between them, and a word near a keyword that heads no declaration, `matc` for `match`, is read as the keyword over the word, each when the top-level form then owes nothing. The lowering refuses the word where it stands. A `->` left out between an operand and a returner `-F` after it is minted between them when the top-level form then owes nothing, so a signature short of its arrow owes that arrow alone. An attribute whose `@[` is left out leaves a `]` that closes no `[` in its block and that ends its line or stands before a keyword; a `@[` is minted before the first word of the line or the block member that holds the `]` when the top-level form then owes nothing, so the attribute owes its opener alone and its block keeps its members. A block of `doc` entries reads as documentation, so no `@[` is minted before it. A form the parser closed at its end is refused where its written tiles first leave its rule''s shape — an operand after a tile no hole follows, or a second operand in a hole that holds one — naming the tile the rule writes there, not at the close; and a bracket written once too often or left out is refused where the declaration''s layout places it — a doubled opener at itself, a missing closer at the end of its line or before the line that comes back to its indentation, a missing opener at the end of the line its closer answers — when that comes first. A layout block stays open past a line left of its column when the next line comes back to the column, or when the block''s first line stands too far right, as a deleted keyword leaves it; a `)` with no bracket to close leaves the blocks open too, so the fault is refused in its own statement. A line at column zero inside nested layout blocks, such as an arm typed before it is indented, stays in the innermost block where its top-level form then owes nothing but one repair at the start of the line. A line that a word begins at column zero starts a declaration and closes every block. A form''s end tile after an operator with no left operand, the `;` of `def first =  + 1;`, ends its form, and the forms after it keep their reading: every reading owes that operand, so the end tile does not pay for it alone.','surface-parser surface-lowering','crates/surface-parser/tests/acceptance.rs crates/surface-parser/src/parse/place.rs crates/surface-parser/src/parse/gap.rs crates/surface-lowering/src/lower.rs crates/surface-parser/src/label/layout.rs::a_line_left_of_its_block_stays_when_the_next_line_returns crates/workflow-ledger-tasks/src/ledger/recovery.rs::a_layout_block_stays_open_past_a_broken_line_5189 crates/surface-parser/src/parse/gap.rs::a_line_at_column_zero_inside_nested_blocks_stays_in_a_block_5434 crates/surface-parser/src/parse/gap.rs::an_arrow_left_out_before_a_returner_is_minted_5501 crates/surface-parser/src/parse/gap.rs::a_semicolon_after_a_missing_left_operand_ends_the_member_5502 crates/surface-parser/src/parse/gap.rs::an_attribute_opener_left_out_is_minted_4398',NULL,NULL);
